landing at this attitude.
Possibly the most important question revived by the recent airliner ditchings is that
of the feasibility of deSigning airplanes to survive a ditching. A listing of major factors
affecting ditching is as follows:
(1) Bottom damage
(2) Landing attitude
(3) Flap setting
(4) Gear position
(5) Wave heading
(6) Floor strength
(7) Wing location
The damage that is expected in a ditching, the magnitu"
