Sleeves, Bags, Wrappings

The use of glass-fabric sleeves to protect
flammable circuit-breaker housings was shown
previously (fig. 5), as well as the use of glass-fabric
bags to protect electric connectors (fig. 6). Another
method of protecting flammable nonmetallic
materials is to wrap them with nonflammable Teflon
(TFE) film. When using wrap-around nonmetallic
materials for fire protection, care must be taken to
bind the material securely with nonflammable
materials.
