atmosphere of the Apollo.
Analysis of the fire hazard in the spacecraft
disclosed that fire could erupt in areas such as the
back side of the instrument panels. Therefore, the
hand-held fire extinguisher was equipped with a
flexible metal hose which could be inserted into
special apertures in the panels to reach the otherwise
inaccessible fire zones.
