FBI, as it is commonly called, is an aromatic
polyimide fiber which was developed by the Celanese
Corp. for the U.S. Air Force. The fiber has excellent
abrasion resistance, and retains about 75 percent of
its strength at 725° F. The principal use of FBI is for
webbing, tapes, and cords, where flexibility and
resistance to abrasion are the principal requirements.
An example of a FBI application is shown in figure
19.

