widespread.
Results of these three tests indicate that the Teflon overwrap on
wire bundles is safe at a cabin pressure of 6.2 psia in a 100-percentoxygen atmosphere. At l6.2 psia in a 60-percent-oxygenAO-percentnitrogen atmosphere, adequate egress time is available if the spacecraft
is on the launch complex. At a pressure of 16.2 psia in an atmosphere
of 100 percent oxygen, an unacceptable fire results.

