of Ladicote on circuit breakers provides sufficient protection to prevent flame propagation.
Test 206: The results of this test indicated that the Ladicote is
not sufficient protection for the circuit breakers.
Test 306: The results of this test indicated that the Ladicote does
not provide adequate fire protection for the circuit breakers.
These tests indicated that 90 mils of Ladicote applied to circuit
breakers is adequate protection for the flight atmosphere of 6.2 psia,
100-percent oxygen. The protection in a l6.2-psia, 60-percent-oxygen/
1+0-percent-nitrogen atmosphere is sufficient to provide adequate egress
time. In a l6.2-psia, 100-percent-oxygen atmosphere, an unacceptable
fire results.

