APPENDIX C

POLYCARBONATE-DRIP IGNITION TESTER

The procedures for operation of the polycarbonate-drip ignition
tester are as follows.
1.

Polycarbonate ignitors are fashioned as shown in figure C-l.

2. The polycarbonate is mounted so that the 0.25- by 0.50-inch
section is in the ignitor holder.
3. A 1- by 2-inch tissue paper is wrapped around a Nichrome wire
and placed adjacent to, but not under, the bottom of the polycarbonate
ignitor.
h.

A test specimen approximately 3.5 by 7 inches is prepared.

5. The test specimen is draped in the sample holder, and all
edges are covered to prevent edge ignition.
6. The tester with the sample is placed in the vacuum chamber and
the appropriate connections are made.
T. The chamber is evacuated and backfilled with oxygen to the
desired pressure.
8. -The Nichrome wire is heated electrically until the tissue paper
ignites. The tissue paper ignites the polycarbonate.
9. After the polycarbonate ignites, the vibrator, which causes the
molten polycarbonate to fall on the test sample, is activated.
10.

The sample is observed for burnthrough or ignition.

