APPENDIX D

FLASH-POINT AND FIRE-POINT TESTER

The procedures for operation of the flash-point and fire-point
tester are as follows.
1. A sample of the material (liq_uid, grease, or solid) is mounted
in the test stand, and the needle electrodes are adjusted to the required
dimensions over the sample surface.
2.

The furnace is placed on the test stand.

3. The test stand with the sample is placed in the vacuum chamber
and connected to the temperature programer wiring.
U. The chamber is evacuated and backfilled with oxygen to the
desired temperature.
5. The temperature programer is adjusted to heat the sample at the
desired constant rate.
6. The spark-actuating equipment is set to provide a spark or the
desired energy over the sample at preset time or temperature intervals.

