b u r n e r s . For a given s i z e , shape, and temperature of apparat u s , t h e r e e x i s t l i m i t s o f ambient temperature, p r e s s u r e , f u e l oxidant r a t i o , and d i l u e n t c o n c e n t r a t i o n beyond which q u a s i s t e a d y flame propagation i s n o t p o s s i b l e . 1 - 7 Beyond t h e s e
e x t i n c t i o n c o n d i t i o n s , q u a s i s t e a d y flames cannot be e s t a b l i s h e d
on burners o r caused t o propagate through long t u b e s .
