S h u t t l e Laboratory.
Although drop tower f a c i l i t i e s have
played an important r o l e ( e . g . , Refs.5 and 33) i n previous
g < l experimentation, they impose s e v e r e l i m i t a t i o n s on t h e
s i z e and time s c a l e s f o r combustion experimentation. Typicall y , experiments i n drop towers a r e l i m i t e d t o time s c a l e s of
less t h a n 5 sec and t o t a l space allowances ( i n c l u d i n g
a u x i l i a r y instrumentation) o f l e s s t h a n 5 f t . Many important
combustion experiments cannot be executed p r o p e r l y under t h e s e
c"
