combustion experiments cannot be executed p r o p e r l y under t h e s e
c o n d i t i o n s . These include’ such important phenomena a s autoi g n i t i o n o f single-phase and two-phase combustibles, thermok i n e t i c o s c i l l a t i o n s and cool flames, flape propagation and
e x t i n c t i o n i n single-phase and two-phase combustible systems,
s t a b i l i t y and s t r u c t u r e o f smoldering a r r a y s of p a r t i c u l a t e s ,
high-pressure flame propagation and e x t i n c t i o n processes, and
o t h e r s . The small times a v a i l a b l e f o r drop tower experimentat i o n s are p a r t i c u l a r l y l i m i t i n g .

