The Space S h u t t l e Laboratory o f f e r s a boxcar-sized
f a c i l i t y f o r long-time (hours/days) combustion experimentation.
One may l i s t t h e d i v e r s e a r e a s of combustion experimentation
where p i v o t a l o b s e r v a t i o n s are needed, which have n o t been
o b t a i n a b l e otherwise: 1 ) a u t o i g n i t i o n f o r l a r g e (and/or highp r e s s u r e ) single-phase ( o r two-phase) premixed combustible
systems; 2) s i n g l e (or two-phase) premixed flame propagation
and e x t i n c t i o n l i m i t s over a range o f apparatus s i z e and
p r e s s u r e s ; 3) noncoherent flame propagation; 4) upper p r e s s u r e l i m i t combustion phenomena and i g n i t i o n , propagation, and

