Space s t a t i o n s o f t h e f u t u r e w i l l have many areas o f concern i n v o l v i n g
s a f e t y . The n a t u r e o f t h e o p e r a t i o n o f space s t a t i o n s w i l l r e q u i r e t h a t s a f e t y
be o f paramount importance t o ensure crew s u r v i v a b i l i t y and m i s s i o n c o n t i n u i t y .
Space s t a t i o n s w i l l be designed as o u t p o s t s on a new f r o n t i e r : space. l h i s
f r o n t i e r i s hazardous and u n f o r g i v i n g . Mistakes i n t h e o p e r a t i o n o f a space
s t a t i o n o r t h e p r e d l c t i o n o f c o n d i t i o n s and hazard s c e n a r i o s c o u l d have v e r y
s e r i o u s consequences. Space s t a t i o n s w i l l have l o n g l i f e t i m e s , l i m i t e d capab i l i t y f o r rescue, e x t r e m e l y hazardous o p e r a t i n g environments, crewmembers who
w i l l n o t be a s t r o n a u t s , and a complex s e t o f o p e r a t i n g procedures. The p o s s i b i l i t y f o r mishaps t o occur i s v e r y r e a l .
