Fire-spread
mechanisms
not associated
with
the
surrounding
flow
field
arise
uniquely
in low gravity.
In the burning
of plastic
materials,
heat transfer
to
the surface
induces
bubble
formation
within
the molten materials.
Bursting
of these
bubbles
releases
jets
of vaporized
fuel
into
the surrounding
air
and
may also result
in the ejection
of flaming
particles.
Trajectories
of the flaming
particles
are not dominated by gravity
(i.e.,
the particles
do not fall
to
the floor),
and this
can result
in the deposition
of
