Of the 32 candidate proteins for
USML-1, one-third have flown on
previous flights. Examples of two
candidate proteins and their importance are Neuramiriidase, an
enzyme on the surface of the
influenza virus that enables the
virus to spread in the body, and
reverse transcriptase, an enzyme
