will be used to gain a better understanding of their biological functions and may be of value in the
design of drugs used as specific
treatments for the diseases associated with these proteins. Other candidate proteins may lead to a better
understanding of the immune system, diseases, protein processing in
the body, and the activation/deactivation of individual genes. The proteins that will be flown are selected
a few months before launch.

