gravity: causes of surface
movement in free liquids, the
degree of contact between a
liquid and its container, bubble formation and movement,
and the comparative strength
of subtle forces during fluid
processing. They also
demonstrate techniques for
deploying liquid drops in
microgravity.
Three combustion science experiments examine
the important role of subtle
forces that are usually
masked by Earth's gravity.
