Question: (h'an Calton, UCLA): In transport processes, one is usually interested in number density an ti a
mean diameter. Your eleclron micrographs show shapes as far from spherical, and one has tlJ wonder what
the ""mean diameter"" represents.
Answer: We consider soot particulales as aggregates of near-spherical primary parlicles. The shapes, as
referred to in the question, are shapes of aggregates. The mean diameters, as referred to in the paper, are
mean diameters of the near-spherical primary particles.

