A two-temperature model is described here. where the temperature of
the fuel-particles is different from the temperature of the gas.
However the
size of the fuel-particle is assumed to be small enough so that its velocity is
nearly equal to the gas velocity.
A general treatment of flame propagation
supported by volatile fuel-particles should consider both radiative and
molecular transport mechanisms. the temperature difference and the
differences in velocity between the gas and the particulates, the
nonadiabaticity of combustible systems of finite size. as well as the detailed
kinetics of oxidation and the kinetics of vaporization pyrolysis.
This work has
the somewhat limited aim of examining the interplay of vaporization kinetic
and oxidative kinetic processes for cases where nonadiabatic and radiative
transport mechanisms are not substantial.

