Equations (5) and (6) relate the potential field to the temperature distributions in the gas phase. In the
calculation the sample is irradiated and auto-ignited at the center by continuous thermal radiant flux with
a Gaussian distribution. Far from the surface, <1>, T and Y i must decay to their ambient initial values. T
