approximately 300 11m. This droplet size was very close to the suspending fiber bead size,
however, so fiber interference effects were no doubt important.
For the same oxygen concentration and fuel as shown for the test in Fig. 2, but higher pressures
(0.3 atm), rnicroexplosions were observed. A sequence of frames from before, during, and after a
microexplosion are shown in Fig. 3. In the beginning, droplet burning was nonnal, but then the
liquid disruption begins and fmally the explosion. After the explosion, nonnal droplet burning
