the objections to venting are that the venting flow temporarily enhances the burning rate in microgravity (ref. 9), the final total pressure for guaranteed fire suppression
is unknown, and the stores of
makeup atmospheres
for reconstitution
after venting are limited.
The Space Station Freedom is an international
program, with Japan and the European
Space
Agency (ESA) each contributing
pressurized
laboratory
modules in the final space-station
configuration. The international
laboratories
will be assembled after the MTC, but their development
