systems
and intermodule
ventilation
flows. All three international
partners
now agree on a carbon dioxide
system for fire suppression, with many details equivalent
in principle to those established
for the U.S.
modules.
There are, however, some primary design and operational
differences.
Most of these variations do not affect safety, but one discrepancy
is of concern.
Because of possible system icing and
limited pressure-relief
capacity, the suppressant-flow
system cannot deliver the required quantity of
carbon dioxide in one minute in the ESA module. A maximum release-time
specification
of 30 minutes
