experiments
because
the duration of the second stage
is shortened by the increased rate of heat transfer produced by natural convection,
or the
gas-velocity

and surface-tension

variations

under

natural

convection

may have

promoted

internal liquid mixing and thereby narrowed the region of staged burning.
