zone.
At the
reaction
zone,
the
former
is dominant,
which
results
in a decrease
of the
smolder
temperature
in microgravity.
Away
from
the
reaction
zone
the
latter
is dominant
and
the
temperature
increases
due
to the
lack
of convective
cooling.
All these
effects
are
less
noticeable
as the
flow velocity
is increased,
and as the reaction
propagates
toward
the
sample
interior
confirming
that
buoyancy
is important
at low
