The
above
results
point
out to a smolder
process
that
is
controlled
by the competition
between
the supply
of oxidizer
to
the reaction
zone
and the loss
of heat
from
the reaction
zone.
The presence
of two smolder
controlling
mechanisms,
chemical
kinetics
and heat
losses,
has been
suggested
before
by Ohlemiller
et.al.
[1,9,12]
in a study
of the
effect
of oxygen
concentration
and pressure
on the smolder
of polyurethane
foam.
To understand
how these
two controlling
mechanisms
affect
the characteristics
of the smolder
process
is convenient
to analyze
