Results and Discussion:
1. Thin Fuel:
1.1 Spread Rate: The experimental flame spread rates, VI,eXPt' over the thin cellulosic fuel in five different
quiescent environments, at three different ambient pressures and two oxygen levels, are plotted in Fig. 2.
Su~erposed on this figure is the prediction from the de Ris theory [3], V""deRis' the prediction from a non-radiative

computational model similar to that of Frey and T'ien [4J, VI,non-rad' and, the prediction from a radiative model [5].
Th~ non-radiative models over-predict VI by almost a factor of 2 to 3. Moreover, the clear trend seen in the
exp~riments,

an increase in VI with P00' is completely missed by these models. The model with radiation
pro~uces the best agreement (within 10%) with experiment.
