3.3

Soot Morphology Measurement Technique
The morphology of soot aggregates will be deternUned by performing thermophoretic sampling experiments [Megaridis and
Dobbins, 1988]. Thin ribbons of copper mesh grids will be rapidly inserted into the flame to obtain instantaneous distribution of soot
morphology. Temporal variation of the soot will be determined by inserting different ribbons"
ntrs:19960008386,ntrs,The 3rd International Microgravity Combustion Workshop,,65,"of copper mesh grids will be rapidly inserted into the flame to obtain instantaneous distribution of soot
morphology. Temporal variation of the soot will be determined by inserting different ribbons at pre-determined times. Subsequent
analyses will involve obtaining transmission electron micrographs and analyzing the radius of gyration using a non-subjective digital
image processing technique that was developed as part of this project [Choi and Zhou, 1995).
