Vg

from the ignition source. Note that the EST predicts a spread rate very close to the computations for high
while the de Ris formula, unable to capture the hydrodynamic effects, overpredicts the spread rate by almost an

Vg

order of magnitude. The discrepancy between the EST and numerical model computations grows as
is
reduced and radiation effects beCome dominant, radiation being absent in the EST. With the external radiative
flux imposed, Vf jumps as can be expected, the jump prOviding an indication of the level of importance of
radiation, which can be directly compared to experiment.
