The tests were performed at the air pressure in the compartment of about 660 mm mercury. The oxygen
partial pressure of 152 mm mercury corresponded ~o its 23 % concentration.
The results presented in this work will be refined and analyzed after the video tapes are returned to earth
and the video recording of the experiments is treated by computer.
Conclusion
The aims of the pilot experiments on combustion of materials aboard the ""Mir"" space station has been
mainly achieved. The installation has demonstrated its suitability for conducting investigations of
combustions of non-metal structural materials under microgravity. The results obtained show that
combustion of materials ceases when the velocity of forced flow diminishes, i.e. there is a limiting
admissible velocity of ventilation flows at which arising combustion zone extinguishes. The work
accomplished is a substantiation to proceed experiments on investigation of parameters of combustion of
non-metal structural materials on both the existing ""Mir"" space station and the ISS ""Alpha"" under
development.
