To date, studies have relied on sequential point-by-point interrogation of the soot field. Such methods are not well
suited to investigations involving nonrepeatable time dependent or transient phenomena. In the context of
microgravity combustion science, where constraints on overall experiment duration and/or available expendable
resources are often encountered, this limitation can be difficult to overcome.

