8 = E{3-3 exp (-{3/T,), where f3 ~ 1 is the activation energy parameter and Tf is the flame
temperature for complete combustion, is 0(1). The reduced Damkohler number 8 plays an.
important role in this description. The inner structure for a steady one-dimensional flame
has been discussed by Linan [7]; it depends on two parameters 6 and ""Y. (Of practical interest
is 171 < 1; depending on its sign ""Y stands for the fractional excess of heat that is conducted to
the fuel or oxidant side of the reaction zone). Numerical integration of the structure equation
reveals the dependence of the combustion field on these parameters. The Burke Shumann
limit is recovered when 6 -;-+ 00. By reducing 6 a small leakage offuel and/or oxidant develops
and the flame temperature decreases. This behavior persists with the reactants leakage and
the flame temperature reduction increasing continuously, until extinction occurs at 6 = 6 .
