of the DARTFire
project are to uncover
the underlying
physics
and increase
understanding
of the mechanisms
that cause flames to propagate
over solid fuels against a low velocity
of
oxidizer flow in a low-gravity
environment.
Specific objectives are 1) to analyze
experimentally
observed
flame shapes, measured
gas-phase
field variables, spread rates, radiative characteristics,
and solid-phase
regression
rates for comparison
with previously
developed
model prediction
