UV-Visible

Imaging

As part of the DARTFire sounding
rocket experiment,
an intensified
array video camera is used to image the
flame. This technique
has the advantage
of increased
sensitivity
over film (equivalent
film ASA numbers
can be
as high as 180,000 [5]) and therefore
can enable direct visualization
of radical species by incorporating
appropriate
filters. It has the disadvantage,
however,
of imaging
only in black and white due to its operational
characteristics.
Because
a color image is strongly desired, in part for comparison
with previous
film images,
a
multispectral
intensified
array camera was obtained
(RGB) as well as narrow-bandpass
filters for specific
to obtain

a 24-bit

color composite

image

that could image
excited species.

