Although
most soot aggregates
are submicron
in size, the
primary particles (20 to 50 nm in diameter)
are
in the Rayleigh
limit, so the extinction
(=absorption)
cross section
of aggregates
can be
accurately
approximated
[5-7] by the Rayleigh
solution
as a function
of incident
wavelength,
particles'
complex refractive
index, and particles' volume fraction.
