formation
and promotes
soot oxidation.
(iii) The
dilution and radiative
heat losses caused by the
increase in the concentration
of combustion products
reduces the flame temperature which in turn reduces
the soot formation
rate and the flame luminosity.
This effect is clearly evident
from the incident
radiation measured
