diffusion, for microgravity and for ground controls. There was a clear increase in average and largest sizes
of crystals grown by dialysis in nucrogravity compared with around controls, as seen in table 2 and figures
I and 2. In the best of the three free interface diffusion reactors. the largest crystals (fig. 3) were three to
five times the volume of the best crystals produced in either laboratory on Earth. In both cell types some of
the largest thaumatin crystals measured more than 2 mm from apex to apex of the tetragonal bipyramids.
