Mg/4nR'. When these stresses exceed the yield stress of the crystal, the crystal breaks. Dendritic arms are
sheared off even more readily. For a crystalline solid the yield stress, a ,, _pG, where G is the shear modulus
and typically R=10-' to 10- 4 . Taking M=(4n/3) R 3Amp. G-xkT/a o3"
