7. DISCUSSION
As noted by Ackerson and Schatzel, all the requisite thermodynamic and transport quantities are
known within a reasonable degree of approximation for hard spheres. Thus, we evaluate the growth exponent for the diffusion-limited case as a function of the supersaturation A, the instantaneous radius X, and
the wavenumber j with the following expressions suggested by Ackerson and Schatzel (A&S):
