Data Reduction
After flight, the particulate collected on the thermophoretic probes were analyzed using a
Transmission Electron microscope (TERI) to determine primary and aggregate particle dimensions.
The remains of the samples were weighed to determine their mass loss. The digital data was
transcribed fiom the video record and analyzed to determine the response of the detectors. Once the
flight mass loss rates were determined, 1-g operation conditions to produce the same loss were
determined. These conditions are being used to produce a l -g comparison data set.

