onset of turbulence likely. Turbulent flow involves interactions between many degrees of freedom
over wide ranges of spatial and temporal scales and thus cannot be adequately simulated with
present computer technology. Attempts have been made at reducing complexity by eliminating
inessential degrees of freedom, e.g., on the basis of observations of organized structures (eddies)
in turbulent flows at low Re I1 ). Proper orthogonal decomposition (POD)12), in particular,
represents the fluctuating velocity field u(r,t) by the sum over a denumerably infinite set of POD
modes {cp}m)(r)} that are functions of position r

