The MHD model suggests that this effect was caused by cavitation. The calculations show a
locally reduced pressure in the recirculation loops; this reduction would give a negative local
pressure for a heating field corresponding to 225V (Fig. 6). This local state of hydrostatic
tension provides a driving force for cavitation. The collapse of bubbles then promotes the
nucleation of the solid phase.

