the slightly undercooled melt were obtained. It should be pointed out that no anomaly in 't l or cp
similar to VIT 106 could be observed. The same holds for the measurements performed by the
Fecht group on two bulk glass forming alloys of different composition.
Other ground based work includes analysis of solidification microstructure and phase
selection in the flight specimen (VIT 101) solidified from the undercooled liquid under mg
conditions. Comparison will be made with a I-g reference specimen, as well with those phases
crystallizing at high undercooling by heating the glass into the undercooled melt. Results of an
