which will actually counteract the Marangoni flow. For small imposed vertical temperature differences, a steady-state condition will finally prevail where the vortices generated by the two counteracting forces co-exist and deform the temperature contours near the bubble as shown in Fig 6a
and 6b. For larger temperature differences the fluid flow and temperature fields can go through a
