I

applied. Also, a magnetic field is effective in damping flows induced by g-jitter with larger
component and lower frequency. Further studies also show that the applied field is more effective
in suppressing the flows associated with g-jitter with lower frequencies but only has a moderate
effect on the high frequency g-jitter flows.

