gravity levels of the LG region. However, for a more quantitative comparison of exact
gravity levels on e.g., the weld-pool shape, the interpretation of the transition effect must
be considered. To study fundamental effects of gravity on the stainless steel welds, the
following metallographic techniques were employed: optical microscopy (OM), scanning
electron microscopy (SEM), and scanning transmission electron microscopy (STEM).

