Preliminary Results
Recent analysis on Fe - 18Cr - 8Ni welds demonstrated that the weld-pool geometry was
changed considerably with the variation of gravitational force during KC-135 aircraft
experiment:
(i) The average width of the weld-pool was observed to increase by -10 % and the average
depth was decreased by -10 % at high gravity (RG) compared with those at low
gravity (LG) as indicated in Fig 3. The macrographs (a) and (b) in Fig 4 show the
cross-section of the weld-pool developed in the two different gravity levels. The depth
to width ratio of the weld-pool was observed to be -0.38 at RG and -0.44 at LG. The
