4. SUMMARY

I

Direct observations were taken during crystal growth of lead bromide samples
doped with 500, 5000 and 10000 ppm silver bromide in 1-g conditions.
Stationary solid-liquid interface was flat. When we started growth by moving the
ampoule at a velocity lower than critical velocity of interface breakdown, the
interface got depressed and the shape of depressed pit varied with the velocity.
It became sharply pointed and then slowly formed the instability pulling down the
central part of the interface. When the translation rate was increased, the
interface broke down. The data showed that the theoretically predicted stability

