4. SUMMARY
We have obtained some strong evidence for the correlatIOn between high pressure pulses
and the onset of nucleation of ice in supercooled water. A semi-quantitative analysis based
on the effect of pressure on the displacement of the freezing point provides an explanation
for such a phenomenon. We are also currently pursuing a number of potentially effective
non-invasive measurement methods for the viscosity and surface tension of highly viscous

633

supercooled liquids. Methods based on rotational dynamics appear to be the most
scientifically interesting on the point of view of the fluid dynamical processes.
