Virtual Spaceflight Chamber Concept:
Certain spaceflight experiments can be recorded in holograms in such a manner that having the
holograms on earth is optically equivalent to being back in space with unlimited time to view the
experimene. Properly exploited, this concept can save a significant amount of experiment time
in space by effectively bringing the experiment optically back to earth
Figure 1 illustrates the concept. Holograms of the space flight chamber are produced in space
with a time resolution that is sufficient to capture any movement that is of interest to the
investigator. In this case the chamber includes a growing TGS crystal surrounded by a fluid that
has been seeded with polystyrene tracer particles of three sizes, 200, 400, and 600 micron
diameters.
