In normal gravity, viscous and gravitational forces almost always dominate the motion of a
sphere. In microgravity, many common cases exist in which normally negligible terms in the
equation of motion become important. 6 A complete understanding of the equations allows us to
understand the motion of particles in a fluid as well as to choose experimental parameters in a
new experiment to advantage, leading to special cases of the equations that will govern the design
of the experiment.

