the melt motion are linear, so that accurate predictions of the melt motion for any history
of residual accelerations can be obtained by the superposition of the independent solutions
for (1) the steady or mean component of the residual accelerations\ (2) g-jitters which are
the random fluctuations of residual acceleration from its mean value2,3, and (3) isolated
spikes of much larger accelerat"
ntrs:19990040241,ntrs,NASA Microgravity Materials Science Conference,,577,"teady or mean component of the residual accelerations\ (2) g-jitters which are
