The cause of the periodic nature of the UIS signal
seen in Figure 5 is uncertain,
however it is suspected
that it may be the result of convection cells within the
foam. The convection cells subtly effect the strength
of reaction,
causing
it to produce
more or less
gaseous
combustion
products
that are known
to
attenuate sound waves differently
[13,14].
It is the
fluctuations
in gas concentration
within these cells
that may be attributed the received signal fluctuations.
Future microgravity
