Remarks
An
ultrasound
imaging
system
has
been
developed
and
implemented
into
the
ongoing
Microgravity
Smoldering
Combustion
experiments.
The data collected will provide further insight into the
smoldering
process
and provide
a non-intrusive
method for studying a smolder reaction propagating
through
a permeable
material.
The method
has
successfully
imaged both the reaction front and the
preceding
water condensation
front.
Further, a new
ignition procedure has been implemented
which more
accurately
simulates
a smolder ignition hazard and
allows for a larger portion of the sample to under-go
self-supporting
smolder.
