Combined, these two regimes, Damkohler and radiative extinction,
form a flammability
boundary for
single decane droplets in 50 kPa total pressure, with varying oxygen mole fraction ambients.
Between these two
extinction regions lies an area classified as flammable. A quasi - steady flame should exist within this boundary.
The two branches,
Damkohler and radiative extinction, meet at a minimum oxygen mole fraction.
Based on
Figure 1 we estimate this minimum point to be between 14 and 14.5% oxygen mole fraction. Two tests showed
ignition and flame extinction outside the proposed flammability limit. For these two tests the burning was a result
of ignition transients.
