3.2

Imaging the flame spreading
The transition processes

from ignition to flame spread were investigated

by recording

video

and 35mm still camera images during the experiments. The surface view of the flame spreading
over the charting material was recorded by video and an edge view of the flame shape was
recorded using very sensitive film in the still camera.
The nominal fuel sample is a piece of ashless filter paper which has a area density of 80
g/m 2 and a width of 50 mm (for 2D geometry) or 85mm (for the 3D geometry).

A 1 cm by 1

cm grid is marked on each sample surface as a scale reference.
