as the distance between the burner tip and the
axial location where darkening of the luminous
zone started to occur. On the other hand, the
corresponding flame heights in 1-g were easier
to measure because of the closed tip of the 1-g
flames [5]. Table 1 lists the luminous flame
heights determined in this manner. Naturally,

