mm; (B) r <* 2.3 mm; and (C) r «• 2.8 mm. In
effect, these micrographs represent soot microstructure near the flame axis (A), on the soot
annulus (B), and outside the soot annulus (C).
Figure 4A (flame axis) reveals the presence of
small diffuse background particles, identified as
soot precursor particles in [21, 22]. These particles appear to coexist with larger aggregates

