In general, the ionization
detector
is sensitive to
relatively small particles, and it is well suited for detecting
a flaming fire. The photoelectric
detector is sensitive to
relatively large particles, and it is well suited for detecting
smoldering fires. In microgravity,
smok"
ntrs:20000120278,ntrs,Progress in Fire Detection and Suppression Technology for Future Space Missions,,6,", and it is well suited for detecting
a flaming fire. The photoelectric
detector is sensitive to
relatively large particles, and it is well suited for detecting
smoldering fires. In microgravity,
smoke particles tend to
agglomerate
due to the lack of buoyant motion, to form
larger entities.
This suggests that the ISS detector will
respond faster than the STS detector in microgravity.
