Sample
systems
being
investigated for this research include, hollow
latex spheres (air filled with index of refraction of
1.0), zinc sulfate (ZnS) spheres with index of
refraction of 2.4, and other metal particles such
as titanium dioxide (TiO2) with even higher
indices of refraction. This choice of particles
poses a problem with regard to particle
densities.
Because
particle
densities
vary
between 1.0 for air filled particles to 4.1 for the
ZnS particles (and even higher for other metal
particles), settling and sedimentation occur on
earth, influencing the formation of crystal growth.
This influence will be greatly reduced in a
microgravity environment.

