to inaccuracies [Bedir 1998]. The transmittance of a gas volume is defined as the fraction of the incident
energy that passes through the gas volume. In the absence of reflection and scattering, then the
transmitted energy along a path is the incident energy minus the absorbed energy. The average
transmittance of an isothermal and homogeneous gas over path length (s'-s) of a molar fraction A'hand
