impinging on a flat surface. They tbund that, for ignition, radical quenching retards the system due to the
kinetics of the surface reaction. Extinction is also retarded due to thermal feedback from the
recombination of radicals at the wall.
The investigators propose a mechanism that involves removing H, O, OH, HO2, and H20_ radicals at the
