are similar. We address results for the intermediate formaldehyde separately.
Individual radical sink: Results indicate that individual radical recombination at the surface has little to
no effect on the flame compared to the inert surface case. We examined formaldehyde separately because
of its unique role in the kinetics of the flame. Plots are of no use in examining the results because the
differences are indistinguishable from the inert case. We therefore present the data in tables for sample
stretch rates. Table 7-3 and 7-4 illustrate results at the two extremes of the domain, where any differences
