transparent top of the test section. The flow above the sample (between sample and top of test
section) was subsequently exhausted to the downstream ambient atmosphere.
The flow system provided low flow velocities from 1-30 c d s in the test section. The bulk
velocities in the test section could be estimated during the course of each test. This was possible
due to the O-ring system used to seal the MSU Rig. PreliminGy testing indicated that higher
flow velocities than those used in the thin fuel NASA drop tower tests (above 6 c d s ) were
fill times for low flow rates
