At the beginning of each test, the needle valve flushed the test section with oxidizer at a
higher flowrate than the test condition for instabilities. Higher flow rates were needed because
the top of the test section acts as a heat sink for the flame. When an even flame front was
established, the needle valve was closed until the flame fron
