Science experimentation
on
the ISS.
The FCF is being designed for a ten-year life with the
ability to extend that life to fifteen years through
hardware maintenance
and hardware replacement.
The
goal of FCF is to be able to accommodate
a minimum
of ten experiments
per year in each of the areas of
Fluids Physics and Combustion
science.
The primary mission of the FIR is to accommodate
experiments
from five major.fluids
physics disciplines:
Complex Fluids; Multiphase
Flow and Heat Transfer;
Interfacial
and Capillary
Phenomena;
Colloids,
and
Dynamics and Stability.
Furthermore,
FIR's flexibility
(i.e. large v"
