Electrical Subsystem
The Electrical Power Control Unit (EPCU) is the heart
of the electrical subsystem.
All power from ISS will
flow through the EPCU. The EPCU will provide power
management
and control functions,
as well as fault
protection.
The EPCU will take 120 VDC from ISS
power bus to provide six 120 VDC 4 A and forty-eight
28 VDC 4 A fault protected
circuits to the FIR and
payload hardware.
Payload hardware will have access
to three of the 120 VDC circuits through connectors
located near the left front rack post and six of the 28
VDC circuits at the PI power/data connectors, shown in
Figure 6, on the optics bench.

