The Ignition System consists of two independent
replaceabl e hot wire ign iters opposed 180 deg,
controlled by individual actuators.
The ignition
wires are 4mm diameter lo ops of Kanthal A- I wire,
30 A WG (American Wire Gauge). Each loop is
mounted to a ceramic structure. The assemb ly is
fully replaceable. The ceramic igniter sleeve has two
pins that mate with two sockets on the ignite rmounting interface. This interface is fixed to the
igniter motors. These motors move the igniters into
the deployment area in precise linear steps and then
quickl y retract the igniters after ignition .
The
Ignition System is shown in Figure 10.

The Droplet Deployment System consists of two
