the end without flow (tests 1.0 and 1.1). The char, with forced flow in normal-gravity (test 2.1), was also
about 1 cm from the end. The pyrolysis zone, with forced flow at either gravity level, reached to (or
nearly to) the end of the foam, unlike the quiescent tests. A close inspection of the samples from test 2.x
has also revealed significant concentrations of tar at the fan end of the sample, again particularly in
microgravity.
In the upstream end of the foam, the forced flow had a minimal effect in microgravity. The
mm)
