CONCLUSIONS
Some conclusions from the present experiment are as follows.
1. Although steady thermocapillary flow was observed, the vapor bubbles generated by the epoxy
fillet disturbed the flow before it became oscillatory so that the critical temperature differences were
not determined. However, indications of oscillations were seen in some tests.
2. The flow remained steady even at Ma which was 7.8 times larger than the 'critical' Marangoni
number determined in our ground-based tests, which shows that the Marangoni number is not the

707

appropriate parameter to describe the onset of oscillations.
