B. Results on Unknown Files
Some recorded files haven’t any information about the axes orientation in the KVANT 2 module,
but the crew has noted that the CMG was running at nominal speed. In this case, the classification tool
has found one and only one solution for the axes distribution. In an other files the crew has noted that
during the measurement recording, the CMG was running at nominal speed. The classification has
detected the right event during the first minute and then has found the unknown type. After a
spectrogram analysis, it was possible to see the CMG speed decreasing.

CONCLUSIONS
The Microgravity Environment Classification Tool is adapted to the post-processing of a great
deal of data on which we have enough information to realize a classification data base. The first tests
obtained with this tool are promising in regard with the good results already reached. The data base
organization allows very easy modifications without changing the classificationperformances.

