ABSTRACT
The Orbital Acceleration Research Experiment (OARE) instrument performance for the STS 50
mission is described, with particular attention given to bias calibrations and bias stabilify. The STS 50
mission results show extremely stable sensor output, resolving the in-flight anomalies from the STS 40
mission. In order to determine absolute acceleration levels on the shuttle to frequencies well below I Hz,
instrument driffs with respect to several variables need to be modeled and removed from the data. Since
OAR€ is the firsf accelerometer system to include a complete calibration subsystem, the OARE resuMs
will define how the miniature electrostatic accelerometer (MESA) operates over 14 day missions.
