high angular rate measurement.
With each calibration data set is recorded the sensor temperature, the average deviation of the
sample, and the 'Q' statistic value. The temperature is provided for extrapolation of calibration results
between calibration activities. The average deviation and ' '
a statistic provide a measure of the noise in
the background environment when the sample was taken.
In-flight calibration assumes the input signal does not shift significantly during the calibration and
the sensor output settles quickly to a new input level after a table movement and change in amplifier
range. The OARE software design allows for some modifications to the calibration sequence, frequency,
data set length, and table positions th"
