1. EXPERIMENT LOCATIONS
The experiment camer for USML-1 was the Spacelab. The Orbiter center of gravity was about
(1091.9"", -0.4"", 374.07 halfway through the mission. The Passive Accelerometer System (PAS)
measured the quasi-steady acceleration environment of the Flight Deck and Spacelab on USML-1. A
description of the PAS and PAS results is given elsewhere in this document. Three SAMs heads
recorded data in the Spacelab in Racks 3, 9, and 12, see Table 1 for locations. The OARE sensor was
located at (1153.28"", -1.33"", 317.817. Note that all locations are given in Orbiter structural coordinates,
see Fig. 1. Quasi-steady accelerations and vibrations measured by these accelerometers are discussed
in the following section.

