with the payload.
We now consider a transient event: four astronauts, each massing 80 kg, push off the wall
of a module of Space Station and coast to the opposite end eight meters away. In this case, we
use conservation of momentum to calculate that the Space Station would move the opposite
direction 4 x 80 kg x 8 m

