Two pumps were housed in the common
sump of the flame ducts. The smaller was a 150-gpm
unit and would be used to pump uncontaminated rainwater out of the flame ducts into a series of drainage
channels which, ultimately, released the water into a
man-made ditch on the south side of the site. (This
ditch has become overgrown with vegetation and willow trees over the last 15 years, and is now designated
as a wetland.)

