13. ABSTRACT (Maximum 200 words)

The Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) is one of two racks in the Fluids and Combustion Facility on the International
Space Station. The CIR is dedicated to the scientific investigation of on-orbit fire suppression, fire safety, and space
system fluids management supporting NASA’s Exploration of Space Initiative. The CIR hardware was modal tested and
the CIR finite element model updated to satisfy the International Space Station model correlation criteria. The final crossorthogonality results between the correlated model and test mode shapes was greater than 90 percent for all target modes.

