The comparison shows that the cryogenic system will put approximately 2,000"
ntrs:20050215300,ntrs,The 2004 NASA Faculty Fellowship Program Research Reports,,44,"l payload can be put on the moon based on the delta IV-Heavy
transporting the LCL to TLI. The results were as follows:

X-5

The comparison shows that the cryogenic system will put approximately 2,000 pounds
more usable payload on the moon; however, the hypergolic system is more reliable.
When the cost estimation relation is added on, the best system will be chosen. As for
now, the best system is obviously the cryogenic model, which also gives the ability to use
the liquid hydrogen and liquid oxygen residuals as water if needed.
