The ply lift boundaries on the cone interior wall were isolated by an edge tracking algorithm, and
the total reduction of the cone’s inner diameter over time was measured. Dividing by two yield
the average ply lift height as plotted in Figure 5. The reduction begins at 2 seconds, and then
increases quickly to a plateau at 15 seconds. The ply lift process is noticeably more abrupt in
comparison to the charring depth plots of Figure 4.
