Conclusion
Real-time radiography has been demonstrated as an effective way to observe ply lift dynamics
during hot firing. A series of corrective techniques for X-ray tube intensity fluctuation, detector
fixed-pattern noise, and photon counting noise followed by background subtraction and contrast
enhancement yield an image sequence that is enhanced for human interpretation. Automated
analysis by edge tracking allows ply lift dynamics such as lift height and charring depth to be
quantified over time.
