applying a small quantity of a ferrofluid (FerroTec EMG 909) to their surface. The ferrofluid
used in this case had particle sizes of 10 nm and viscosity of less than 5 cp. The ferrofluid is
generally used to reveal the possible magnetic domain structure of a sample. This method is a
well recognized tool in the field of magnetic domain analysis and is known as the Bitter method.
