b. Purchase of commercial adaptations of open-source tools allowing for technical
support for as long as warranted.
Off-the-shelf computing nodes may not be acceptable because of their large footprint. I
recommend using semi-customized, off-the-shelf computing nodes in order to save space.
As indicate in Figure 2, space is a resource requiring constant attention.
A small 5 to 10 node Beowulf proof-of-concept system should be evaluated for both a
simulation and IVHM.
Ask reflective memory vendors to show their wares on the above system.
Complete simulation/test of architectures; verify simulation accuracy of systems.
Verify simulation test-bed against representative workloads.
Use simulation test bed to study advanced application workloads and to set requirements
for IVHM and future simulation.

