European Columbus module
The European Columbus module will be added to ISS
during a Shuttle flight in late 2007, and has the
capacity to house 10 pressurized research racks
within the module and four external payloads on the
Exposed Payload Facility (EPF) (Figure 3) [7].
Based on interagency agreements, ESA and NASA
each has rights to five racks and two external payload
sites. The first five racks, all European-built, will be
launched inside Columbus, and two external payloads
will be launched and repositioned to the EPF during
the same flight. Four of the five NASA racks are
already on orbit and will be relocated from Destiny to
Columbus, while the fifth will arrive on a later
Shuttle flight and be installed directly in Columbus.
