refrigerator/freezers, and food warmers. One or two
more MELFI racks may also be added, to support an
expanded demand for cold stowage and to serve as
on-orbit backups for the first MELFI freezer. To
support transportation of conditioned samples, active
and passive units will be available (Table 3). Active
units include the MERLIN (Microgravity Experiment
Research Locker/Incubator) single-middeck locker
sized refrigerator/incubator and the Glacier (General
Laboratory Active Cryogenic ISS Experiment
Refrigerator) double middeck locker sized
refrigerator/freezer. Both MERLIN and Glacier can
also be placed in ExPrESS Racks for on-orbit
operations. Passive units include Single and Double
Cold Bags, aerogel-insulated devices that use phase
change materials for thermal mass.
