SUMMARY
With its assembly more than halfway to completion,
ISS is already a productive platform for conducting
research in space. The next few years will see the
addition of several pressurized modules, truss
elements and solar arrays to greatly expand its
capabilities. By the end of this decade, ISS will
become the envisioned human outpost in space
bringing together many nations for the benefit of life
on Earth and as a bridge to future exploration.
