Structure & Liftoff In Combustion Experiment
(SLICE)
The SLICE experiment investigates the structure of
lifting and lifted flames, where flow conditions and the
combustion chemistry cause the flame to detach from
the burner and stabilize at a downstream position. The
twin purposes for the SLICE research are increased fuel
efficiency and reduced pollutant emission in practical
combustion devices. More explicitly, the experiment is
being conducted to advance combustion modeling

