Spacecraft Fire Safety
Spacecraft fire detection provides significant challenges compared to terrestrial conditions because the
properties of the smoke emitted from fires is affected by
buoyancy. The conditions on a spacecraft require rapid
detection of fires with limited false alarms. Two recent
experiments examine issues related to spacecraft fire
detection. The Dust Aerosol measurement Feasibility
Test (DAFT) [3] examined the background aerosol
particulate levels on the ISS. The Smoke Aerosol
Measurement Experiment (SAME) [4] examined the
particle size distribution of the smoke from spacecraft
materials. These instruments can provide useful guidance for the designers of future spacecraft smoke
detectors.

