The infrared camera used in the tests was a 12 bit FLIR Systems, Inc. Prism DS™ with a 50 mm
lens. A 200 nm bandwidth ‘flame filter’ centered at 3.8 μm was used to remove most of the gasphase radiation from CO2 and H2O. The surface temperature calibration was p"
