<p>Impacts of estimated plume rise on PM2.5 exceedance
prediction during extreme wildfire events: a comparison
</p>
<p>of three schemes (Briggs, Freitas, and Sofiev)
</p>
<p>Yunyao Li1,2, Daniel Tong1,2,3, Siqi Ma1,2, Saulo R. Freitas4, Ravan Ahmadov5,6, Mikhail Sofiev7,
Xiaoyang Zhang8, Shobha Kondragunta9, Ralph Kahn10, Youh"
ntrs:20230009908,ntrs,"Impacts of Estimated Plume Rise on PM<sub>2.5</sub> Exceedance Prediction During Extreme Wildfire Events: A Comparison of Three Schemes (Briggs, Freitas, and Sofiev)",,1,"schemes (Briggs, Freitas, and Sofiev)
</p>
<p>Yunyao Li1,2, Daniel Tong1,2,3, Siqi Ma1,2, Saulo R. Freitas4, Ravan Ahmadov5,6, Mikhail Sofiev7,
Xiaoyang Zhang8, Shobha Kondragunta9, Ralph Kahn10, Youhua Tang2,3, Barry Baker3,
</p>
<p>Patrick Campbell3, Rick Saylor3, Georg Grell6, and Fangjun Li8
