the next droplet, a new ﬂame was formed around the
next droplet. This observation is somewhat different
from the results in normal gravity by Kato et al. [12].
Our analysis discussed the dependence of the ﬂame-
spread rate on the droplet spacing through a simpliﬁed
model that monitored the rate-controlling processes.
We plan a detailed discussion in future work by con-
sidering the temporal variation of the ﬂame radius.
