and conductive losses are obtained by integrating the heat of reac-
tions, radiative and conductive ﬂuxes. Figure 8 show that the inte-
grated heat generation has a very sharp rise during ignition of the
stratiﬁed premixed fuel/oxidizer surrounding the droplet initially.
A rapid decrease in heat generation occurs during transition to dif-
fusively controlled burning. The decrease in Qgeneration after ignition
is in part a consequence of the increasing radiative loss Qradiation
during the ﬁrst stage of the burn as the ﬂame radius increases with
time (Fig. 3). The radiative heat loss is almost a factor of 2 higher
