excessive droplet vaporization pushing the ﬂame outward. The
mixture near the droplet surface in which the rich ﬂammability
limit is exceeded grows, and transition to the classical high temper-
ature quasi-steady diffusion ﬂame occurs as the mixed fuel vapor
and oxygen is consumed. Figures 10–12 shows the development
