perature and low temperature burning. During the ﬁrst stage com-
bustion which is governed by high temperature kinetics, major
products are CO2 and H2O (Fig. 16a). But as transition to the second
stage occurs, the peak CO2 decreases drastically and CO concentra-
tion increases. The prominence of CO further establishes the fact
