4.1. Damkohler number analysis 
The critical Damkohler number (Da crit) analysis presented here 
is applied to both blowoff and quenching sides of the ﬂammabil- 
ity boundary since ﬁnite rate chemistry applies along the entire 
ﬂammability boundary. For both blowoff and quenching, the Da crit 
becomes too small: At blowoff, the ﬂow rate is too large to allow 
the relatively fast reactions to occur, while at quenching, the reac- 
tion rate becomes too small due to slow mixing of the reactants. 
