4.3. Surface energy balance 
To examine the role of radiation and solid phase conductive 
losses on the ﬂame, a surface energy balance is developed. A two- 
zone surface energy balance schematic for the rod tip is formu- 
lated as shown in Fig. 18 to account for the 3D nature of the 
ﬂame over the nearly spherical tip of the rod. Zone one is the 
area deﬁned by the hemispherical tip of the rod. The entire zone 
is assumed to be at the pyrolysis temperature T s , consistent with 
the observed bubble layer length from Fig. 5 , and consistent with 
Bi << 1 from Eq. 4 heat ﬂux levels. Zone two is the cylindrical rod, 
with an interface to Zone 1 at the base of the hemisphere. Only 
solid conduction loss out of Zone 1 into Zone 2 is considered, us- 
ing the rod cross sectional area while the other terms use the tip 
hemispherical surface area, which is twice as large. 
