E-mail address: paul.ferkul@nasa.gov (P. Ferkul). 
the ﬂammable mixture of pyrolyzate and oxygen. Thus, the ﬂame 
propagates in a creeping fashion as a series of ignition steps where 
the ﬂame acts both as the source of solid heating and ﬂammable 
gas ignition [1–4] . The intricate coupling of processes in the solid 
and gas-phase is strongly dependent on various space and time 
scales. For ﬂame spread, the relevant space scales may include 
sample size (length, width, thickness) and conﬁnement size (con- 
tainer or tunnel dimensions), while the relevant time scales may 
