strates the effects of ﬂow acceleration due to thermal expansion 
during conﬁned combustion. Compared with the inversely propor- 
tional relationship between spread rate and tunnel height (V f ~
1/D) predicted by Li et al. [10] , the spread rate increases slower 
when D decreases, due to a decreasing local ﬂow rates. For the re- 
