[8] . In their work, 1 mm thick, 5 cm wide, and 20 cm long PM- 
MAs were burned next to a wall. For a conﬁned condition similar 
to that in Fig. 6 (sample-wall distance = 2.5 cm), the ﬂame was 
observed to continually accelerate throughout the burning process. 
This accelerating ﬂame spread was due to the increasing buoyancy 
ﬂow induced by the ﬂame during the burning process and was 
