and slightly smaller volumetric heat capacity ( ρ• C p ∼1.44 vs. 
2.46 J/cm 3 /K). Therefore, the ﬂame heat loss to the duct window 
is expected to be smaller than the heat loss to the baﬄe. This con- 
tributes to a stronger ﬂame at H = 3.8 cm. 
