to the sample surface exhibit non-monotonic dependency on the 
baﬄe distance, H. However, the heat loss to the baﬄe increases 
monotonically when the baﬄe distance decreases. When the baﬄe 
is far from the ﬂame, e.g., H > 1.5 cm, the heat loss to the baﬄe 
is negligible compared with the ﬂame heat transfer to the sample 
surface. When H decreases to 1.0 cm, heat loss becomes compara- 
