show that a blue flame tip extending beyond the glare surrounding the 
ignitor. This is an ignitor-supported ignition (27). Premature turning off 
of the ignitor can quench the flame since there is still too high of a heat 
loss rate to the solid (i.e. qc > qcmaximun) [28]. At 124 s, the ignitor 
