CA1 described above. The TEOM was calibrated using mass stan-
dards supplied by the manufacturer, and the volumetric ﬂow ca-
librated with an independent, traceable standard. The calibration
of the SMPS was veriﬁed with reference Polystyrene Latex Spheres
(PSL). The Diameter of Average Mass (DAM) shown in Table 1 and
plotted in Fig. 7 is computed as the ratio of the measured mass and
number concentrations.
Data records from a representative test run are shown in Fig. 5.
As seen from the temperature proﬁle, the tube heater is ramped
up and held at the speciﬁed peak temperature until the 7 min
mark. As indicated by the arrow inserted above the abscissa, this
produces an interval of roughly 5 min in length where the outputs
of the two MPASS channels are essentially constant. The number
concentration as measured by the CPC exhibits a curved trajectory,
and spans a range of roughly 27% of its peak value over this same
interval. The aerosolized mass production rate as recorded by the
TEOM remains essentially constant throughout the duration,
