One of the remarkable aspects of these expressions is that the
spread rate is independent of opposing ﬂow velocity Vg for thin
fuels while it is proportional to Vg for thick fuels. An increase in Vg
obviously raises the heat ﬂux (W/m2) from the gas to the solid, but
it also shortens the preheat zone length, making the heat ﬂow
(W) independent of ﬂow velocity. This heat is used to raise the
