along the length of the sample, followed by flame regression. The exception is 40 kPa in normal gravity, in which the average flame spread was less than 0.5 mm, 
and most of the combustion took place in the flame regression phase.
Fig. 4. Curves showing the depletion of oxygen over time in microgravity (left) and normal gravity (right) for four ambient pressures. The dots on each curve 
