The classical Lewis number (Le) is a well-established parameter 
governing thermo-diffusive instabilities, which are known to induce 
fingering patterns in smoldering combustion [24]. Although the com­
bustion of PMMA in this study is characterized by gas-phase reactions 
rather than solid-phase smoldering, we hypothesize that Le remains the 
dominant governing parameter for the observed flame splitting, pro­
vided the phenomenon is driven by an analogous thermo-diffusive 
mechanism. To capture this behavior, we adopted the effective Lewis 
