Crucially, transport properties such as gas density (ρg), oxygen mass 
diffusivity (DO2), and gas-phase thermal diffusivity (αg) exhibit signifi­
cant pressure dependence. Furthermore, the thermal thickness (δ) relies 
on the flame spread rate (Vf), which is also highly sensitive to ambient 
pressure. By evaluating these pressure-dependent properties at the local 
ambient conditions for each experimental data point, the proposed Leeff 
effectively normalizes the influence of pressure on the flame spread 
dynamics. Table 1 lists the parameter values used in the calculation of 
Peeff and Leeff.
