1.3. Scale Analysis 
The relative importance of radiation in the previously described 
opposed ﬂow ﬂame can be determined by scaling arguments to 
vary strongly with ﬂow velocity. In order for the ﬂame to achieve 
steady state, the solid fuel must vaporize, combust, and transfer 
heat into the upstream virgin fuel all within the residence time 
of the ﬂow in the leading edge of the ﬂame which scales with the 
diffusion length scale L g ≈
