3. Results and discussion 
The gas-phase is solved over a nonuniform grid of minimum 
size 432 by 120, with higher grid density in the preheat and py- 
rolysis regions in the x-direction and in the surface boundary layer 
in the y-direction. The bounds of the region of heightened grid 
density are manually adjusted for each ﬂame to include the pre- 
heat region, pyrolysis region, and burnout location, if it occurs. As 
the ﬂow velocity increases, the number of grid points is manu- 
ally increased and the domain size is reduced, though the devel- 
opment length of the ﬂame is held consistent at 122 mm. In all 
cases the results are tested for grid and domain (in the down- 
stream and freestream directions) independence. A typical com- 
putation time is an hour for models without feedback and up to 
