Fig. 3. Edge view ﬂame tracking data from a 24%
oxygen, 6.4 psia, 30 cm/s concurrent test. Both sides of
the ﬂame are tracked. The ﬂame base remains anchored
near the igniter wire from 2 to 2.5 s as the ﬂame tips
grow rapidly. The base accelerates and after 3.5 s reaches
a steady spread rate for the remainder of the drop. The
tips slow their spread rate at about 3.5 s and the ﬂame
reaches a constant overall length by 4 s into the drop,
and maintains that length for the remainder of the drop.
Spread rates are derived from the linear sections of the
left and right ﬂame base tracks, and result in ﬂame
spread rates of 15.97 and 15.64 mm/s.
