deﬁne opposed ﬂow as positive, and concurrent
ﬂow as negative. The x-axis displays the relative
velocity between the ﬂame and forced ﬂow,
deﬁned as the imposed forced ﬂow velocity plus
the ﬂame spread rate; the latter is always positive.
Thus, the ﬂame spread rate increases the relative
velocity
for
opposed
ﬂow
conditions,
and
decreases it for concurrent ﬂow conditions. For
