As the forced opposed-ﬂow speed is increased, the
ﬂame spread rate also increases very rapidly, but
only to about 10 cm/s. Further increases in the
opposed ﬂow velocity do not change the ﬂame
spread rate. Since this dependence had been
shown previously [11], in this work we focused
on concurrent conditions where less data are
available.
On the left side of Fig. 4 the corresponding
