by previous investigators wherein the ﬂame spread
rate was found to correlate with (O2)0.9(P)0.05,
with oxygen in mole-fraction and pressure in
atm. [14]. The near-independence of spread rate
with pressure is in agreement with [15], where
for inﬁnite kinetics and negligible heat losses the
spread rate is independent of pressure and forced
ﬂow velocity. We found that our new data, as well
as previous data from both normal and micro-
gravity, were well correlated by this relationship
except near the limit. The results are shown in
