6. Computational results 
The mathematical model consists of the two- 
dimensional, steady, elliptic, partial differential 
equations describing conservation of energy, 
species mass, total mass, and momentum in the 
gas phase and ordinary differential equations 
for the conservation of mass and energy in the 
solid phase. In the numerical model, the gas and 
solid phases, coupled through interface condi- 
tions, are solved sequentially using the SIMPLER 
algorithm. A single-step global reaction with 
second-order kinetics is used in the gas phase and 
a first-order pyrolysis kinetics is used in modeling 
fuel vaporization. Details of the model, including 
the properties used, can be found elsewhere [19] , 
