is much larger and the visible flame is much more 
intense. The length of the computed flame (about 
40 mm) closely matches the top view of the flame 
in size, which is shown at the same scale. In the ki- 
netic regime close to blow-off extinction, the flame 
length can be seen to decrease to a narrow strip in 
both computations and experiment. Although not 
shown in a separate figure, as the fuel thickness is 
