To realize microgravity conditions [34] , the 
COSMOTORRE drop tower (in Hokkaido, Japan) 
was used. The microgravity duration is about 2.5 s, 
and the gravity level is more than 10 −3 G 0 . The ex- 
perimental set up was installed into a drag shield 
capsule to suppress the decrease in the quality of 
the microgravity condition. When the capsule vi- 
bration was dumped at the top of the tower, a 
droplet was generated by remote control and the 
capsule was released. A trigger signal was sent by a 
μg-sensor to the high-speed video camera and the 
droplet elevator to start recording backlit images of 
a droplet and to insert a droplet into the electric fur- 
nace, respectively. The microgravity experiment was 
performed once for each ambient condition. 
Fig. 5. Sequential backlit images of an evaporating 
droplet in supercritical environment. 
3. Results and discussion 
Figure 5 shows sequential images of a droplet 
evaporating in the supercritical environment. The 
droplet placed at the test position was vibrated for 
about 0.035 s. Such vibration continued longer at 
the higher ambient pressures. Since the droplet sus- 
pension fiber is thin, the droplet was very spher- 
ical. The droplet size increased in the beginning 
owing to the heat expansion, and then decreased 
owing to evaporation. After 0.835 s, the droplet 
size decreased quickly. In the middle of evap- 
oration, a droplet evaporating at high pressures 
was surrounded by dense fuel vapor, as shown in 
