(M. Mikami). 
acteristics in premixed combustion have actively 
been studied using counter flow burners and micro- 
reactors [1–2] . The appearance of cool flame in 
non-premixed combustion has also been studied 
[1–2] . 
There are several studies reporting that the cool 
flame appears in droplet combustion. Tanabe et al. 
[3–4] experimentally showed that the cool flame 
appears in auto-ignition of droplets at high tem- 
peratures and pressures and there are different 
