3. Results and discussion 
3.1. Phenomena near the flame-spread limit 
Fig. 2 shows the flame-spread behavior near 
the flame-spread limit. The flame-spread limit is 
the dimensionless droplet spacing beyond which 
the hot flame no more appears. In Fig. 2 a, the 
flame spreads to Droplet L from the flame sur- 
rounding Cluster H, which consists of Droplets A 
and B. The dimensionless distance from Droplet 
A to Droplet L is S AL / d 0 = 15.7. On the other 
hand, in the case of S AL / d 0 = 19.8 shown in Fig. 2 b, 
the flame does not spread to Droplet L. There- 
fore, the condition in Fig. 2 b is outside the flame- 
spread limit. Mikami et al. [17,20] obtained the"
