flame-spread limit from a single burning droplet, 
FSL1 = ( S / d 0 ) limit , and ( S / d 0 ) limit = 14 for n -decane at 
room temperature and atmospheric pressure. Oy- 
agi et al. [18] demonstrated that the flame-spread 
limit with strong droplet interaction is greater than 
FSL1. Mikami et al. [19] proposed the flame-spread 
limit from an imaginary droplet with twice the 
mass at the center of the mass of two droplets, 
FSL2 = 2 1/3 ( S / d 0 ) limit = 17.6 as an approximation of 
that from burning two droplets with strong inter- 
action. Yoshida et al. [13] showed that the flame- 
spread limit from the center of the mass of two 
droplets with strong interaction is slightly smaller 
than FSL2. 
We now discuss the phenomena appearing 
around a droplet existing outside the flame-spread 
limit. The relationship between a diffusion flame 
surrounding a droplet and the next unburned 
droplet basically determines the flame spread over 
droplets. In the flame spread between droplets at 
relatively low ambient temperature, the heat from 
a diffusion flame transfers to the next unburned 
droplet, a flammable mixture layer forms around 
the heated unburned droplet, the auto-ignition of 
a part of the flammable mixture layer causes the 
premixed-flame propagation through the layer, and 
finally a new diffusion flame is formed [17] . There- 
fore, a flammable mixture layer possibly forms 
around the droplet existing outside the flame- 
spread limit. Mikami et al. [15] conducted flame- 
spread experiments to simulate the large-scale igni- 
tion and reported that a similar phenomenon to the 
large-scale ignition occurs when fiv e droplets e xist- 
ing outside the flame-spread limit are heated by a 
flame and are then ignited by another flame spread- 
ing from another route. This suggests that a large 
amount of flammable mixture is generated around 
the droplets existing outside the flame-spread limit. 
Fig. 3 demonstrates that a droplet existing out- 
side the flame-spread limit is ignited by another 
flame spreading from another route. Since Droplet 
L is not ignited at the end of the burning of Cluster 
