envelope flame with a very interesting structure. The flame tail spreads
outward, but an inner weaker flame is also formed as indicated in the
figure. This inner flame is connected to the downstream outer flame but
extends backward and ends close to the solid surface. This inner flame is
attributed to the recirculation zone behind the sphere (Re ~ 1300)
where the oxygen recirculates back to the rear of the sphere and reacts
with the fuel vapors that may otherwise escape to the ambient. In Case
