where both (Sz/SL)0 and Ma can be derived from linear fitting, depicted
as dashed line in Fig. 10(e) for NPF and in Fig. 11(a) for PPF. In this
context, (Sz/SL)0 represents the intercepts of fitted lines, while the Ma
corresponds to the slope. Fitting results show a decrease in Ma, indi-
cating that a diminishing control of the strain effect. Notably, at the final
stages of PPF extinction (0.99 text in Fig. 11), Ma even approaches
negative to near zero. The reduction of Ma suggests that the strain effect
tends to decrease its influences on flame propagation during extinction
so that the extinction must gradually shift to radiation-controlled be-
haviors towards the end.
Since heat from the radiative PPF region is generated from reaction
heat release and lost through radiation effect and transported to the
unburned region, correlations between Qrad/Qrea and DaL are presented
in Fig. 10(f) for NPF and Fig. 11(b) for PPF. Linear fits for Qrad/Qrea and
DaL using Eqn. (6) are shown by dashed lines in the figure.
