This expression is used here only as an interpretive relation, rather than 
a predictive model for the present data [18].
The increase of the measured effective LOC-FS with diameter is 
consistent with prior work showing that smaller PMMA cylinders spread 
faster because the unburned solid is easier to preheat and the convective 
boundary layer around the cylinder is thinner, while more recent scaling 
analyses show that cylindrical spread differs from flat-fuel spread 
through curvature enhanced heat transfer and the role of forward solid 
conduction [7–23].
For a cylindrical solid fuel of diameter d, the convective contribution 
can be expressed in the standard form 
