The oscillatory character of the hot-flame extinction has been discussed previously (Dietrich et 
al., 2014; Liu et al., 2016). After hot-flame extinction both droplets burn for a prolonged period 
of time with a cool flame, as evidenced by the nearly linear behavior of the droplet history. For 
both droplets the cool flame burned for a longer period of time than the hot flame. The cool 
flame surrounding both droplets extinguished at a finite droplet size, as indicated by the vertical 
dashed lines in Figure 1. For the decane droplet, the imaging system stopped recording before 
the cool flame extinguished. The 
