KEYWORDS
Flame length; Flame spread;
Microgravity ﬂames; PMMA
Introduction
Small scale ﬂames have been largely studied by researchers all over the world for the
last four decades, for their importance in ﬁre safety, ignition transients in solid
propellants, and basic understanding of combustion phenomena (Wichman, 1992;
Williams, 1976). In order to isolate the inﬂuence of particular parameters on diﬀer-
ent ﬂame characteristics, researchers focused on diﬀerent burning conditions, i.e.,
varying oxygen level or imposing a forced ﬂow. In this work we consider an
opposed-ﬂow conﬁguration in order to investigate the boundary layer eﬀect on
spread rate and length of ﬂames burning along thin sheets of polymethyl-
