The gas phase model
The gas phase of the numerical model consists of Navier-Stokes equations for laminar
ﬂow and conservation equations for mass, energy and species. A one-step global reaction
equation is considered.
For PMMA fuels, pyrolysate is considered as MMA vapour with a chemical formula
C5H8O2. The reaction occurs between fuel vapour and air at stoichiometric conditions
and produces only carbon dioxide, water vapour and nitrogen. The reaction equation for
PMMA fuel combustion is written as follows.
C5H8O2 + 6(O2 + 3.76N2) →5CO2 + 4H2O + 22.56N2
(4)
All the gaseous components obey the ideal gas law. The thermal and transport properties
for each species are obtained from a standard reference. The gas-phase thermal radiation
is assumed to come from carbon dioxide and water vapour only. The solid radiation is
assumed to be diffuse. The formulated non-dimensional form of the governing equations
for the gas phase model is as follows.
