( < 5 cm/s). At 23% oxygen concentration, the ﬂame spread rates are higher than the ﬂame
spread rate values for 21% oxygen. Here, the ﬂame spread rates increase and decrease with
an increase in ﬂow speed, similar to the trend reported for thick PMMA rods [12]. Both
in 21% and 23%, the ﬂame does not spread for the ﬂow speed of less than 2 cm/s, and
as the ﬂow increases, the spread rates increase and peak around the ﬂow speed of 5 cm/s
and decrease with a ﬂow speed up to 25 cm/s. Also, the microgravity ﬂame spread rates
are higher than corresponding normal gravity ﬂame spread rates, with more considerable
differences noted at low ﬂow speeds.
To understand the effect of ﬂow on the ﬂame spread process, the ﬂame is represented
by an area enclosed by a reaction rate contour of 10−4 g/cm3 s, temperature contour lines
