diffusion enhances the ﬂame, causing the ﬂame to be stronger. Consequently, this promotes
the ﬂame spread. However, the importance of these two competing effects depends on the
width of the tunnel. When the tunnel is narrow, lateral heat loss from the ﬂame becomes large
