ﬂame and affect the entire ﬂame. As the tunnel becomes wider, there is less conductive loss
(compared with total heat release) but the oxygen cannot reach the middle of the ﬂame by
side diffusion. The computed results in ﬁgure 9 suggest that the oxygen side diffusion, acting
mostly in the upstream ﬂame based region, can overpower lateral heat loss, most pronounced
