EVALUATION OF DROPLET SIZES FROM 
IMAGES 
In this analysis we determine the edge 
coordinates at a number (N) of points. A circle is 
then fit to these points and the diameter of this 
circle is taken to be the droplet diameter. This is 
the approach used by Dembia et al. (2012) for 
evaluating sizes of droplets that are strongly 
sooting, though Dembia et al. (2012) did not 
consider diffraction or partial coherence effects. 
For the circle fit procedure, we follow the 
analytical procedure of Kasa (1976). We provide 
some of the details of this analysis below because 
Kasa (1976) derived a best-fit equation for the 
radius R of a circle, while we are interested in a 
best-fit equation for R2. This is because R2 is 
needed for calculating burning rates. 
