Experiment
The suspended droplet experiments were conducted in a drop-
tower facility described previously.1,11,19,20 Approximately 1.2 s of
free fall was available, which restricted droplet sizes to less than
1 mm for observingthe completeburning historyin the low-gravity
environment at atmospheric pressure. The gravity level was about
10¡ 4g/g0 (where g0 =9.8 m/s2) in the moving frame of reference
because a drag shield was used. The droplets were suspended from
