allowing the particles to coagulate.  After a specified aging time, the smoke was then pushed by the piston into the 
diagnostics duct where the moment instruments 
made their measurements. Also installed in the 
diagnostics duct were space shuttle and ISS 
smoke detectors.  As the smoke was monitored 
by the moment instruments, a sample of the 
smoke particles was deposited on Transmission 
