According to the phenomenology, the following simplifying assumptions can be adopted:
1.
The gas supply tube does not affect the evolution of the SDF.
2.
All processes are spherically symmetric.
3.
The porous medium in the ﬂow region can be modeled by ﬂow resistance according to
the Darcy law and heat exchange with the ﬂuid according to the Newton law, i.e., the
porous medium can be represented by added momentum and heat sources,
