11.
Soot particles are the clusters of 20–25 carbon atoms, have the corresponding constant
size, and do not coagulate.
12.
The radiation heat ﬂux is caused solely by soot, H2O, CO2, N2 and O2 emittance.
13.
The outer wall of the chamber is impermeable, isothermal, and non-catalytic.
