with time. The measured and calculated ﬂame temperatures agree satisfactorily with each
other (see Figure 4), and the radiative extinction of ﬂames occurs when the temperature of
both the normal and inverse ﬂames decrease with time to a value of approximately 1200 K.
It is important to note that the model satisfactorily describes both the dynamics of changes
in the ﬂame size and the dynamics of changes in ﬂame temperature. Similar ﬁndings were
reported in [44]."
