intensity early in the burning process. A constant thres-
hold cannot adapt to such changes in surrounding inten-
sity, and such an analysis does not succeed at repro-
ducing the results obtained with Image-Pro. An adap-
tive threshold is necessary for these images. For t > 
0.25 s all four analyses are consistent. Fig. 8b compa-
res the relative errors for the adaptive threshold method 
for toluene for two different values of f. The results 
show that f = 1.0 produces a smaller error compared 
to f = 0.67, as the larger value provides a looser fit.  
 
